cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If Fairbeam contributes to published work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Fairbeam: an open electromagnetic workbench"
abstract: >-
  Fairbeam is a free and open-source desktop workbench for designing and
  simulating antennas and RF circuits on the openEMS FDTD solver. It provides
  a parametric 3D designer and Python models, automatic meshing with design
  checks, CPU and GPU solver engines, sweeps and optimization, far-field,
  array and material analysis, and reproducible run bundles with exports to
  Touchstone, CSV, STL, glTF, Gerber and CST-compatible VBA macros.
authors:
  - given-names: İsmail
    family-names: Akdağ
    affiliation: İzmir Kâtip Çelebi University
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6470-5892"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ismailakdag/fairbeam"
url: "https://fairbeam.org"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - antenna design
  - computational electromagnetics
  - FDTD
  - openEMS
  - microwave engineering
  - GPU
  - reproducible research
